From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 20:52:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: remove collab + collab_ui + call + livekit_* crates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Removes the collab UI stack and its dependencies:
  - crates/collab/            (collab server)
  - crates/collab_ui/         (channels panel, share UI, presence, notifications UI)
  - crates/call/              (voice/video calls, screen sharing)
  - crates/livekit_api/       (LiveKit REST API)
  - crates/livekit_client/    (LiveKit client SDK)

External consumer cleanups:
  - title_bar/: deleted src/collab.rs (collaborator avatars + call controls);
    removed pub mod collab and use call::ActiveCall in title_bar.rs;
    removed 5 methods that wired the title bar into ActiveCall
    (window_activation_changed, active_call_changed, observe_diagnostics,
    share_project, unshare_project); dropped the _diagnostics_subscription
    field and active_call observer subscription; removed
    render_collaborator_list / render_call_controls calls from render().
  - git_ui/git_panel.rs: potential_co_authors() now returns Vec::new() and
    local_committer(room: &call::Room, ...) is deleted. Co-author attribution
    relied on active call participants; with the call stack removed there is
    never a room to attribute against.
  - zed/main.rs: removed use collab_ui::channel_view::ChannelView,
    call::init / collab_ui::init in the boot sequence, and the
    open_channel_notes-handling loop in URL request dispatch.
  - zed/zed.rs: removed channels_panel load, its add_panel_when_ready call,
    and the collab_panel::ToggleFocus action registration.
  - zed/zed/app_menus.rs: removed 'Collab Panel' menu entry and its import.
  - zed/visual_test_runner.rs: removed call::init.

Workspace Cargo.toml: removed 5 member entries and 5 workspace deps. Each
consumer's Cargo.toml: removed call/collab*/livekit_* deps and test-support
features.

notifications, channel, client still present — they will be addressed in
subsequent patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
